					<summary style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--fg-pencil); font-size: 1.05rem;">
						What is the very first thing I should do to change my name after marriage?
					</summary>
					<p style="margin: 0.75rem 0 0 0; font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-color); line-height: 1.6;">
						The absolute first step is ordering 3 to 4 certified copies of your marriage certificate from your county clerk or vital statistics office. Once received, your first legal filing <strong>MUST be with the Social Security Administration (Form SS-5)</strong>. State DMVs, the State Department (Passport), and banks cannot process a name change until your updated identity is registered in the federal SSA database.
					</p>
