						How much does it cost to change your name after marriage in the United States?
					</summary>
					<p style="margin: 0.75rem 0 0 0; font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-color); line-height: 1.6;">
						The total out-of-pocket cost typically ranges from <strong>$80 to $290</strong>. While the Social Security Administration charges $0, you will pay for certified marriage certificate copies ($30–$90 for 3 copies), a new state driver's license / Real ID ($15–$45), a passport update ($0 if issued within 12 months, or $130 renewal fee + $15 photos), and vehicle title updates ($10–$35).
					</p>
				</details>

				<details class="hand-card" style="padding: 1rem; background: #fafafa; border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil); cursor: pointer;">
					<summary style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--fg-pencil); font-size: 1.05rem;">
						Can I travel on my honeymoon under my new married name?
