					</p>
				</details>

				<details class="hand-card" style="padding: 1rem; background: #fafafa; border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil); cursor: pointer;">
					<summary style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--fg-pencil); font-size: 1.05rem;">
						Do I need a court order to take my spouse's last name or hyphenate?
					</summary>
					<p style="margin: 0.75rem 0 0 0; font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-color); line-height: 1.6;">
						In almost all US states, taking your spouse's surname, hyphenating both surnames, or moving your maiden name to your middle name can be done directly using only your certified marriage certificate. A formal court order petition ($150–$450 court fee) is only required if you are inventing a completely new blended surname or altering your first name.
